    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d291">

                <pb facs="0518" n="1976" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p2/pg1976"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320.2–AC/4–2851: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United States Mission at
                        the United Nations </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-04-28T12:00:00-05:00">April 28,
                            1951—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>887. UK Emb informed Dept Apr 27 UK wld agree to AMC mtg <pb facs="0519" n="1977"
                        xml:id="pg1977"/> Apr 30. Added, however, UK wld object strongly to AMC
                    moving quickly and reporting at once to GA First Comite. UK hopes AMC will hold
                    “occasional” mtgs and wishes opportunity for further consultations like those
                    now under way so that prior to preparation AMC report future action may be
                    reviewed in light circumstances then prevailing.</p>
                <p>Emb reps were informed we were arranging AMC mtg with Sarper, probably May 3.
                    Dept reps naturally agreed there must be full discussion of proposals but
                    emphasized Dept view AMC shld now proceed to act. Further details by pouch.</p>
                <p>Reptd info AmEmbassy London 4953.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
